### §9. Get collections stats.
POST http://localhost:1538/stats
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "stress"
}

### ─── §10. Stats ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### ✅ Metrics
GET http://localhost:1538/system/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ─── §11. Application-Side Materialized Index ──────────────────────────────
### MoltenDB has no built-in secondary indexes yet. This section demonstrates the
### documented workaround: use "fields": [] to cheaply collect matching keys, save
### them into a dedicated idx_* collection, then serve future reads with an O(1)
### batch `keys` lookup instead of re-running the filter every time.
### See docs/api-reference.md → "Application-Side Materialized Indexes" for details.

### §11a. BUILD — one-time filter query with "fields": [] to collect matching keys.
### Only "_key"/"_v" are returned per match — no field values, minimal payload.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "stress",
  "fields": [
  ],
  "where": {
    "price": {
      "$gte": 1500,
      "$lte": 2500
    }
  }
}

### §11b. STORE — save the collected keys as the application-managed index document.
### Copy the "_key" values from §11a's response into the "keys" array below.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "idx_price_1500_2500",
  "data": {
    "range": {
      "keys": [
        "stress_998333",
        "stress_998332",
        "stress_998330",
        "stress_998329",
        "stress_998328"
      ]
    }
  }
}

### §11c. READ (1/2) — pull the key array back out of the index collection.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "idx_price_1500_2500",
  "keys": "range"
}

### §11d. READ (2/2) — O(1) batch lookup against the primary collection using the
### key array from §11c. No `where` scan, no sort — just direct DashMap lookups.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "stress",
  "keys": [
    "stress_000001",
    "stress_000042",
    "stress_000913"
  ]
}

### §11e. MAINTENANCE reminder — this index is NOT auto-updated. If a document's
### price changes (or it is deleted), you must rebuild/update idx_price_1500_2500
### yourself, e.g. by re-running §11a and overwriting §11b.
POST http://localhost:1538/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "stress",
  "data": {
    "stress_000001": {
      "price": 9999
    }
  }
}

